WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:02.702
- The head of high school
suggested an alternative,

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.337
which was that I
should only share

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:06.172 align:start size:81% position:19%
white conservative
views on race.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:09.743
So I should only
have conservatives

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:12.345
who had white skin

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:13.279
- Unbelievable.

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:14.414
- Since that would not confuse

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:16.516
or inflame the students.

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:19.085
(gentle music)

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:24.591 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
- I'm Dave Rubin
and joining me today

00:00:24.591 --> 00:00:27.327 line:0%
is a teacher and educator
at Grace Church School

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:29.562 line:0%
in New York City who
recently wrote a piece

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:32.532
on Bari Weiss's
sub stack titled,

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:37.170
I Refuse To Stand By While My
Students Are Indoctrinated.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.205 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then you can guess
what happened next.

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:41.174
Cancel culture came to his door.

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:43.143
Paul Rossi, welcome
to the Rubin Report.

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:45.779
- Thank you, Dave.

00:00:45.779 --> 00:00:47.781 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's a pleasure to be here.
- All right.

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:49.182
So I've wanted to chat with you

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:51.151
since I read the piece,

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:53.219 align:start size:88% position:13%
and we are going to
link to the piece below

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:55.088 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I hope everyone
will read it,

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:56.689 align:start size:81% position:19%
but for people
watching right now

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:59.359
that have no idea
about any of this,

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:01.528
can you sort of sum
up the piece first

00:01:01.528 --> 00:01:03.196 align:start size:84% position:16%
and then we'll kind
of get into everything

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:04.531
that's happened since then?

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:07.000 line:0%
- Sure.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.704 line:0%
Basically, for the last,
I'd say four to five years

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:14.340
there's been an
increasing change

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.642
in the culture of the school

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:19.079 align:start size:88% position:13%
as it started to
implement what it calls

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:21.081
it's anti-racist programming

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:26.019
in the high school that I teach.

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:28.555
So grades nine through 12 there.

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:33.560
And I noticed a series
of very concerning things

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:36.362
were happening there

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:39.432 align:start size:88% position:13%
and basically a
stifling of expression,

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:45.138
to the point where kids
were afraid to be silent,

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:48.108 align:start size:97% position:3%
they were expected to say
things, say the right things.

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:50.977
If they didn't say
the right things,

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:55.482
they were flagged as
problematic in emails.

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:57.083
And a lot of this was designed

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:59.018
to sort of create
a certain culture,

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:05.291 align:start size:84% position:16%
a culture that's
based on critical race
theory, essentially.

00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:08.962
So I started to hear
complaints from some

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:10.797
of the students in the school,

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:12.499
some of my own students,

00:02:12.499 --> 00:02:14.467
some who weren't my students,

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:19.472 align:start position:0%
that this was becoming extremely
uncomfortable and difficult

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:23.676
and really poisoning the
atmosphere in the school.

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:27.547 align:start size:81% position:19%
And I witnessed
some things myself

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:30.450
in meetings that were
segregated by race.

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:33.253
So we would frequently
have whites only meetings

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:36.122
and BIPOC meetings,

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:38.558 align:start size:88% position:13%
black indigenous people
of color meetings.

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:41.594
And so as there was
also a proliferation

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:44.964
of opt in affinity groups,

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:50.970
so basically this notion
that individual opinions

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.042
and ideas had to conform

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:58.745
to your sort of racial
group and gender group.

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:00.847 align:start size:84% position:16%
And when things
differed from that,

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:04.017
it was seen as anomalous

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:07.120
or not representative of
what you should think.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:10.757
And I had some experiences
in classes that I teach.

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:12.725
I'm a math teacher primarily,

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:15.228
but I also teach
a persuasion class

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:17.964 align:start size:84% position:16%
where some of the
students in that class

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:20.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
complained of having sort
of a bubble mentality

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:23.236
and they weren't getting any
of the other types of opinions.

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:26.239
So I suggested to my
head of high school

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:29.242
that maybe we could talk about,

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:31.844
we could bring in
some of the ideas

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.012 align:start size:81% position:19%
of professor Glenn
Lowry at Brown,

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.314
a Brown economist.

00:03:34.314 --> 00:03:36.516 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'm sure you're
familiar with his ideas.

00:03:36.516 --> 00:03:37.450
- Of course.

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:39.452
- Because the students, well,

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:40.687
a lot of our discussion focused

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:43.256
around the protests and
riots over the summer.

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:45.325 align:start size:97% position:3%
So they wanted to maybe
hear an alternative opinion.

00:03:45.325 --> 00:03:46.859
But I was told by my
head of high school

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:48.995 align:start size:84% position:16%
that it would be
extremely problematic

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:54.000
and disruptive to students
of color and other students

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:59.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
if I shared a conservative
views of a black man.

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:00.773
- Right.

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:02.942
To be clear, he happens to
be a black conservative.

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:04.410
- Yes, he happens to be a black,

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:07.380
that was not even in
my initial proposal.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:10.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was simply that he
has certain views on race

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:13.319 align:start size:88% position:13%
and the racial issues
that may differ slightly

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:15.822 align:start size:84% position:16%
from what Grace Church
School is pushing,

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:19.993
sort of a center right,
but still very mainstream

00:04:19.993 --> 00:04:23.296 align:start size:97% position:3%
if you look at the opinions
throughout the country.

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:25.131
And the head of high school
suggested an alternative,

00:04:25.131 --> 00:04:27.200
which was that I
should only share

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.035 align:start size:81% position:19%
white conservative
views on race.

00:04:29.035 --> 00:04:32.572
So I should only
have conservatives

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:35.908
who had white skin

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:37.343
- Unbelievable.

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:39.412 align:start size:97% position:3%
- since that would not confuse
or inflame the students.

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:43.249 align:start size:84% position:16%
So I didn't even
respond to that email.

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:45.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wound up not even
teaching that unit at all.

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:50.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I just, I was so
disgusted by that response

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:53.960 align:start size:84% position:16%
which I just see as
self-evidently racist.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.062 align:start size:84% position:16%
The notion that the
dissemination of ideas

00:04:58.798 --> 00:05:01.134
should be filtered based
on the color of the skin

00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:02.302 align:start size:84% position:16%
of the person who's
speaking them.

00:05:02.302 --> 00:05:04.070 align:start size:88% position:13%
And it's just completely
anti intellectual

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.571
and regressive, in my opinion.

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:08.408
Subsequent to that,

00:05:08.408 --> 00:05:13.179 align:start size:97% position:3%
there was a self care
meeting during the pandemic

00:05:14.547 --> 00:05:16.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was ostensibly
designed to help students

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:19.919 align:start size:84% position:16%
cope with the
struggles and problems

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:21.854
with being at home stuck,

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:23.923 align:start size:84% position:16%
maybe they're not
able to come to school

00:05:23.923 --> 00:05:25.291
more than twice a week.

00:05:26.159 --> 00:05:28.127 line:0%
And in this meeting

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:30.129 line:0%
up came the white
supremacy slide

00:05:31.364 --> 00:05:32.932 line:0%
saying that some of
the characteristics

00:05:32.932 --> 00:05:34.967 align:start size:88% position:13%
of white supremacy
culture included things

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:37.937
like objectivity,
and individualism,

00:05:37.937 --> 00:05:42.008 align:start size:97% position:3%
and most interestingly
enough, a right to comfort.

00:05:42.008 --> 00:05:47.013
So in the segregated
whites only meeting

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:49.682
that was supposed to
be teaching students

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:52.985
how to feel more comfortable

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:55.688
with the events that
were surrounding them,

00:05:55.688 --> 00:05:57.323
they were told that
if they were white

00:05:57.323 --> 00:05:59.525
they should question
their right to comfort

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:01.627
which I found the
height of irony.

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:05.865 align:start size:97% position:3%
So then the facilitator
who was actually very nice,

00:06:05.865 --> 00:06:07.767 align:start size:81% position:19%
we got along quite
well I thought,

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:13.339
asked the group of 200 students

00:06:13.339 --> 00:06:15.174
and maybe 30 of my colleagues

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:16.576
whether they might be feeling

00:06:16.576 --> 00:06:20.012 align:start size:84% position:16%
a white feeling
around these topics.

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:23.983
And at that point, I
decided to question

00:06:23.983 --> 00:06:26.853 align:start size:88% position:13%
what that actually
meant, a white feeling.

00:06:26.853 --> 00:06:28.855
Like, what makes
a feeling white?

00:06:28.855 --> 00:06:33.860
And I was a little
miffed and concerned

00:06:35.261 --> 00:06:36.529
because I thought that
this was blatantly racist

00:06:36.529 --> 00:06:40.600
but I was going to try
to present my questions

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:43.169 align:start size:84% position:16%
in a way that
wasn't antagonistic.

00:06:43.169 --> 00:06:45.405 align:start size:88% position:13%
And later she did
speak to me and tell me

00:06:45.405 --> 00:06:47.907 align:start size:84% position:16%
that she didn't feel
that my questions

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:50.610
were offered in bad
faith or anything.

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:55.415
So what I wanted to do
by asking the question

00:06:55.415 --> 00:06:57.417 align:start size:84% position:16%
was to open up the
discourse a little bit

00:06:57.417 --> 00:07:00.620
so that students may
see me as an example

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:03.589
and maybe model for them that
it's okay to question ideas.

00:07:03.589 --> 00:07:05.358 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's okay to have
different viewpoints.

00:07:05.358 --> 00:07:07.026 align:start size:81% position:19%
And that's exactly
what happened.

00:07:07.026 --> 00:07:10.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
So students in the chat
window of the Zoom meeting

00:07:10.062 --> 00:07:13.299 align:start size:88% position:13%
started to ask a broader
range of questions.

00:07:13.299 --> 00:07:16.969
Even faculty joined in with
some questions of their own.

00:07:16.969 --> 00:07:18.671
The facilitator allowed it.

00:07:20.006 --> 00:07:23.242 align:start size:97% position:3%
So there were a lot of
questions against capitalism.

00:07:23.242 --> 00:07:24.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I put my own idea
about capitalism in there

00:07:24.744 --> 00:07:27.547
which was that capitalism
is extremely anti-racist

00:07:27.547 --> 00:07:31.150 align:start size:97% position:3%
since it's done more to
lift people out of poverty,

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:33.085
lift nonwhite people
out of poverty than

00:07:33.085 --> 00:07:35.354
than any other of
its competitors.

00:07:36.422 --> 00:07:38.791 align:start size:84% position:16%
Some of the questions
that I put in

00:07:40.693 --> 00:07:41.828
also questioned the nature

00:07:41.828 --> 00:07:44.397
of racial identification at all.

00:07:44.397 --> 00:07:46.199
Like, why should I
identify as white?

00:07:46.199 --> 00:07:48.935 align:start size:84% position:16%
Why should I
introject an identity

00:07:48.935 --> 00:07:50.336 align:start size:81% position:19%
based on how other
people see me?

00:07:50.336 --> 00:07:51.704
Why is that necessary?

00:07:51.704 --> 00:07:53.206 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so that comment
and some others

00:07:53.206 --> 00:07:54.574 align:start size:81% position:19%
made their way out
of the meeting,

00:07:54.574 --> 00:07:57.243
sort of violating the
norm of confidentiality

00:07:57.243 --> 00:08:02.181
to some folks that were not
in the whites only meeting

00:08:03.282 --> 00:08:04.784 align:start size:84% position:16%
and caused some
concern and agitation

00:08:04.784 --> 00:08:06.219 align:start size:97% position:3%
and then they had to have
meetings about the meetings.

00:08:06.219 --> 00:08:08.855
And then it was sort
of a week and a half

00:08:08.855 --> 00:08:11.324
of upheaval, processing.

00:08:11.324 --> 00:08:13.025
People felt harmed.

00:08:13.025 --> 00:08:17.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was brought in to speak
to my head of school

00:08:17.096 --> 00:08:18.564
and the assistant
head of school.

00:08:18.564 --> 00:08:22.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was asked how I felt
about what I had done.

00:08:23.669 --> 00:08:25.171
And I actually felt great.

00:08:25.171 --> 00:08:28.374
So I said, "I'm not contrite.

00:08:29.775 --> 00:08:32.011 align:start position:0%
"Apparently people are
claiming that I've caused harm,

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:35.314
"but no one has come to
me to express this harm."

00:08:35.314 --> 00:08:38.918
And they couldn't even
explain the causality

00:08:38.918 --> 00:08:41.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
of how my questions could
have caused the harm

00:08:41.153 --> 00:08:42.522
in the first place.

00:08:42.522 --> 00:08:44.223
And they kept raising the stakes

00:08:44.223 --> 00:08:45.958 align:start size:84% position:16%
when they noticed that
I wasn't contrite.

00:08:45.958 --> 00:08:50.596 align:start size:97% position:3%
And they said, "Well,
you've caused grievous harm.

00:08:50.596 --> 00:08:53.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You've disturbed the
student's peace of mind."

00:08:53.533 --> 00:08:55.801
And then at the end,
when I wasn't contrite,

00:08:55.801 --> 00:08:58.204
they said, "It's raised to
the level of harassment."

00:08:58.204 --> 00:09:00.573 align:start size:88% position:13%
And at that point I
just ended the meeting.

00:09:00.573 --> 00:09:01.641
I had a subsequent meeting

00:09:01.641 --> 00:09:03.276
with the head of
the whole school

00:09:04.443 --> 00:09:07.647
and he reiterated
his disappointment.

00:09:07.647 --> 00:09:11.450
He had some pre-textual
reasons for being upset

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:14.353
but clearly what was
causing the problems

00:09:14.353 --> 00:09:18.791
in the school were the
nature of my questions.

00:09:18.791 --> 00:09:21.027
Not necessarily some of
the pre-textual things

00:09:21.027 --> 00:09:21.994
that surrounded it.

00:09:23.763 --> 00:09:26.032 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Okay, so there
there's a lot there.

00:09:26.032 --> 00:09:28.367
And I know that for
my main audience

00:09:28.367 --> 00:09:29.835 align:start size:84% position:16%
that maybe hasn't
heard about this yet,

00:09:29.835 --> 00:09:31.304
everything you're
saying is probably

00:09:31.304 --> 00:09:32.538
not that shocking to them,

00:09:32.538 --> 00:09:34.507
because I think so
many people have

00:09:34.507 --> 00:09:36.709
now seen this sort of woke thing

00:09:36.709 --> 00:09:40.613
infect so many schools and
high schools and colleges

00:09:40.613 --> 00:09:43.649 align:start position:0%
and now virtually every
institution and everything else.

00:09:43.649 --> 00:09:45.251
So all this is happening.

00:09:45.251 --> 00:09:48.821
And was there a
moment where you,

00:09:48.821 --> 00:09:50.590
like, what was it in
you that was like,

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:51.624
I have to say something now?

00:09:51.624 --> 00:09:52.858
Because I think a lot of people,

00:09:52.858 --> 00:09:53.793 align:start size:81% position:19%
the question of
the day is sort of

00:09:53.793 --> 00:09:55.194
what makes people stand up?

00:09:55.194 --> 00:09:57.330 align:start size:97% position:3%
'Cause I think we're watching
a lot of people fold,

00:09:57.330 --> 00:10:00.032
and I'm glad to see that not
only did you write the piece

00:10:00.032 --> 00:10:01.267
and got in touch with Bari,

00:10:01.267 --> 00:10:03.669 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I'm curious how
that happened as well,

00:10:03.669 --> 00:10:05.671 align:start size:84% position:16%
but then are willing
to do press after

00:10:05.671 --> 00:10:08.407 align:start position:0%
and really keep walking
through the fire on this thing.

00:10:10.376 --> 00:10:13.245 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Well, once it
started to cascade

00:10:13.245 --> 00:10:16.515
I began to feel a real
sense of exhilaration

00:10:16.515 --> 00:10:18.551 align:start size:84% position:16%
and duty that I was
doing the right thing.

00:10:18.551 --> 00:10:21.287
So that carried me through
up until the present day.

00:10:22.688 --> 00:10:25.658
I wasn't sure when I started
to ask what a white feeling was

00:10:25.658 --> 00:10:30.663
or ask these things in the
chat, how it would play out.

00:10:31.397 --> 00:10:32.198
I hadn't planned it.

00:10:32.198 --> 00:10:33.265
It started something.

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:36.535 align:start size:84% position:16%
My impulse to do
those things initially

00:10:36.535 --> 00:10:38.904
was simply to provide,

00:10:40.239 --> 00:10:41.474
those questions were genuine,

00:10:41.474 --> 00:10:43.576 align:start size:88% position:13%
but I asked them because
I felt that students

00:10:43.576 --> 00:10:47.313 align:start size:88% position:13%
needed to see a teacher,
an authority figure,

00:10:47.313 --> 00:10:51.217
model for them how free
discourse is conducted.

00:10:51.217 --> 00:10:54.353 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I hadn't seen
anyone do that before.

00:10:55.821 --> 00:10:57.790
And I felt that this was
something that I could do.

00:10:59.258 --> 00:11:01.994
And as it started to cause
all of this chaos around me,

00:11:01.994 --> 00:11:05.464
I realized, well, this is
actually pretty important.

00:11:05.464 --> 00:11:07.299
And the more chaos was going on,

00:11:07.299 --> 00:11:11.404
the more I actually felt that
it was important to pursue it.

00:11:11.404 --> 00:11:12.772 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah, I mean, it's
so extraordinary

00:11:12.772 --> 00:11:14.440
because obviously,
you know the story

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:16.142
of Bret Weinstein at Evergreen

00:11:16.142 --> 00:11:19.545
and so much of my audience
knows that story of course.

00:11:19.545 --> 00:11:21.380 align:start size:84% position:16%
And we've heard so
many versions of this.

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:23.783 align:start size:84% position:16%
So then how did you
get in touch with Bari

00:11:23.783 --> 00:11:26.285 align:start size:84% position:16%
and how did this whole
article get written

00:11:26.285 --> 00:11:27.887
and the whole piece there,

00:11:29.321 --> 00:11:31.824 align:start size:97% position:3%
the public part of this not
just fighting back internally?

00:11:33.225 --> 00:11:37.697 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Well, my contract, they
offer a contract year to year,

00:11:39.098 --> 00:11:42.635
and so in my current contract
expires the end of August.

00:11:42.635 --> 00:11:44.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I had to sign the
contract for the next year

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:47.139
by April 15th.

00:11:47.139 --> 00:11:50.142 align:start size:97% position:3%
And part of the contingencies
of that contract

00:11:50.142 --> 00:11:54.447
were that I attend a
restorative practices

00:11:54.447 --> 00:11:57.116
designed by the office
of community engagement

00:11:57.116 --> 00:11:59.118 align:start size:84% position:16%
to address the harm
that I'd caused

00:11:59.118 --> 00:12:02.955 align:start size:97% position:3%
students of color and other
students in the school.

00:12:02.955 --> 00:12:05.424
But they would not specify
what those practices would be

00:12:05.424 --> 00:12:06.692
until after I signed.

00:12:06.692 --> 00:12:08.861
So I was in a bind there.

00:12:08.861 --> 00:12:09.829
So I found

00:12:10.796 --> 00:12:12.098
- Incredible.

00:12:12.098 --> 00:12:13.799 align:start size:97% position:3%
- some legal representation
through FAIR,

00:12:13.799 --> 00:12:16.368
the Foundation Against
Intolerance and Racism.

00:12:16.368 --> 00:12:19.205
I spoke with Bari who's
on the board of advisors,

00:12:19.205 --> 00:12:22.942
and she suggested that I write
a piece about my experiences.

00:12:22.942 --> 00:12:26.746
And I wrote 5,000
words at first.

00:12:26.746 --> 00:12:29.448
I had a lot to say. And
then we edited it down

00:12:29.448 --> 00:12:30.649 align:start size:84% position:16%
to something that
was more digestible.

00:12:30.649 --> 00:12:32.418
And then I did another draft,

00:12:32.418 --> 00:12:34.019
and then she had some tweaks.

00:12:34.019 --> 00:12:37.523
So the editing was very helpful,

00:12:37.523 --> 00:12:38.991
but those were all my words.

00:12:40.392 --> 00:12:43.596
And I'm really pleased
with the effect it's had.

00:12:43.596 --> 00:12:45.998
- So, okay, so you
put the piece out

00:12:45.998 --> 00:12:48.234
and then the hate starts coming.

00:12:48.234 --> 00:12:50.970 align:start size:88% position:13%
You get support from
some quarters of course,

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:52.805
but then the hate
starts rolling in.

00:12:52.805 --> 00:12:55.407
And then what's the next
thing that the school did?

00:12:55.407 --> 00:12:57.143 align:start size:84% position:16%
'Cause this is where
it really starts

00:12:57.143 --> 00:12:59.211
kind of going off the rails.

00:12:59.211 --> 00:13:00.346
- Well, it is interesting.

00:13:00.346 --> 00:13:02.915 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, I got
overwhelming support,

00:13:02.915 --> 00:13:06.719
predictably, through
Bari's subscribers

00:13:06.719 --> 00:13:10.289
and through an email
that I had placed there

00:13:10.289 --> 00:13:13.225 align:start size:88% position:13%
but I was curious how
the school was reacting.

00:13:14.527 --> 00:13:16.395
The article came
out on the 13th,

00:13:16.395 --> 00:13:18.664 align:start size:84% position:16%
my contract I had
to sign by the 15th.

00:13:18.664 --> 00:13:20.733
I hadn't gotten
back to them yet.

00:13:20.733 --> 00:13:22.868
And then on the 14th, I believe,

00:13:22.868 --> 00:13:24.703
I received a threat from someone

00:13:24.703 --> 00:13:26.272
within the school community.

00:13:26.272 --> 00:13:27.840
It was not a physical threat

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:30.309
but it was a threat to my
livelihood, my wellbeing,

00:13:30.309 --> 00:13:32.478 align:start size:84% position:16%
and it was basically
everything but

00:13:32.478 --> 00:13:36.215
So I reported the threat
to the administration.

00:13:36.215 --> 00:13:38.017
I reported it to
the head of school.

00:13:39.218 --> 00:13:41.821
And then they tried to
use that as a pretext

00:13:41.821 --> 00:13:43.422
to keep me out of the school,

00:13:43.422 --> 00:13:46.625 align:start size:88% position:13%
to keep me from
teaching in the school.

00:13:46.625 --> 00:13:50.729 align:start size:97% position:3%
Saying that, "Maybe you feel
unsafe because of this."

00:13:50.729 --> 00:13:52.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, "No, actually
I don't feel unsafe.

00:13:52.898 --> 00:13:54.667
"I'm merely bringing
this to your attention

00:13:54.667 --> 00:13:57.136
"to something on your radar
you should take care of."

00:13:57.136 --> 00:14:00.806 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then they tried to reframe
this threat as an opinion.

00:14:01.974 --> 00:14:03.776 align:start size:88% position:13%
And they said they
would poll the opinions

00:14:03.776 --> 00:14:05.044 align:start size:84% position:16%
of the other
students and faculty

00:14:05.044 --> 00:14:08.180
to see if they felt safe
with me in the building.

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:09.915
And so when they came
back to me and said,

00:14:09.915 --> 00:14:11.717
"No, actually your students

00:14:11.717 --> 00:14:12.651
"don't want to be
in your classes

00:14:12.651 --> 00:14:14.753
"so we need to keep you home.

00:14:14.753 --> 00:14:17.623
"And in fact, we're going to
take away all your classes."

00:14:17.623 --> 00:14:18.958
- Unbelievable.

00:14:18.958 --> 00:14:21.393 align:start size:88% position:13%
- So they were
indifferent to my claim

00:14:21.393 --> 00:14:23.195 align:start size:84% position:16%
that actually if
someone makes a threat

00:14:23.195 --> 00:14:25.831
aren't they the ones that
should be staying home?

00:14:25.831 --> 00:14:28.100
Why is the teacher punished

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:30.903
for what another person did?

00:14:30.903 --> 00:14:32.972 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Unfortunately, my
lack of shock is just,

00:14:32.972 --> 00:14:34.673 align:start size:84% position:16%
well, not only because
I know your story,

00:14:34.673 --> 00:14:37.610
but I mean, we know this
story over and over again,

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:40.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
sort of false allegations
then gaslighting

00:14:40.546 --> 00:14:43.749
and reversing accusations
and all of these things.

00:14:43.749 --> 00:14:46.051
Okay, so we're going to
play this audio clip now.

00:14:46.051 --> 00:14:48.153 align:start size:88% position:13%
Can you just set up what
happened between you

00:14:48.153 --> 00:14:50.322
and the head of the school
to give a little context

00:14:50.322 --> 00:14:52.791
and then we'll play
and then come back?

00:14:52.791 --> 00:14:54.360
- Sure.

00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:55.728 align:start size:84% position:16%
So the head of school,
George Davidson,

00:14:55.728 --> 00:14:57.963
sent a letter to
the whole community

00:14:57.963 --> 00:15:02.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
saying that in my article
I had misrepresented

00:15:04.036 --> 00:15:05.271
the conditions at the school,

00:15:05.271 --> 00:15:08.240 align:start size:84% position:16%
that I had substantial
omissions in there,

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:10.776
and they reiterated their
commitment to anti-racism,

00:15:10.776 --> 00:15:15.781
and they relayed to the
school that they had

00:15:16.882 --> 00:15:18.651 align:start size:84% position:16%
offered me this
chance to participate

00:15:18.651 --> 00:15:22.655
in a subcommittee of a committee

00:15:22.655 --> 00:15:24.290 align:start size:84% position:16%
that would be
heavily supervised.

00:15:24.290 --> 00:15:28.894
So, as to sort of try to
co-opt what I was saying.

00:15:30.195 --> 00:15:31.764
However, their claim that I had

00:15:33.165 --> 00:15:35.134
misrepresented things
or left omissions,

00:15:35.134 --> 00:15:37.303
I responded to that
with my own letter,

00:15:38.704 --> 00:15:43.409
saying that I actually had
in conversations with George,

00:15:45.811 --> 00:15:47.479 align:start size:81% position:19%
he had clearly
acknowledged to me

00:15:47.479 --> 00:15:50.783 align:start size:97% position:3%
that he had grave doubts
about the school's own policy

00:15:50.783 --> 00:15:54.186 align:start size:84% position:16%
and that he
specifically had said

00:15:54.186 --> 00:15:55.354
that there was a problem

00:15:55.354 --> 00:15:58.023 align:start size:84% position:16%
with demonizing
whites at the school.

00:15:59.191 --> 00:16:00.693 align:start size:81% position:19%
So I released that
letter publicly

00:16:01.660 --> 00:16:03.062
in response to his letter.

00:16:03.062 --> 00:16:04.730 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then he released
a letter back

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:09.335
saying that this was, in
his words, I misquoted him.

00:16:09.335 --> 00:16:11.503 align:start size:88% position:13%
I attributed to him
things he had never said

00:16:11.503 --> 00:16:13.672
nor would ever say in the press.

00:16:13.672 --> 00:16:16.075
My actions were unprofessional.

00:16:16.075 --> 00:16:19.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
So he was impugning my
character and my veracity.

00:16:19.445 --> 00:16:22.381
So at that point I
felt I had no choice

00:16:22.381 --> 00:16:25.884
but to release clips
of the conversation,

00:16:25.884 --> 00:16:27.152
which I had recorded,

00:16:27.152 --> 00:16:28.954
because I was worried
that it might come up

00:16:28.954 --> 00:16:30.122
in an employment dispute.

00:16:30.122 --> 00:16:32.057 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Right, it's actually
quite incredible

00:16:32.057 --> 00:16:34.660
because you did this
like an absolute pro

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:36.495 align:start size:84% position:16%
in terms of the
emails back and forth

00:16:36.495 --> 00:16:38.163
and then doing this recording.

00:16:38.163 --> 00:16:40.933 align:start size:97% position:3%
And well, let's let the
recording stand on its own.

00:16:40.933 --> 00:16:42.368
So let's throw to that.

00:16:42.368 --> 00:16:44.970 align:start size:84% position:16%
- [Paul] Let me ask
you something, George,

00:16:44.970 --> 00:16:47.539
because I think there's
something very different

00:16:47.539 --> 00:16:49.641
about having a single experience

00:16:49.641 --> 00:16:52.211
where you make sense of it,

00:16:52.211 --> 00:16:54.847
and having a teacher,
an authority figure

00:16:54.847 --> 00:16:58.083 align:start size:84% position:16%
talk to you
endlessly every year,

00:16:58.083 --> 00:17:01.153 align:start size:88% position:13%
telling you that because
you have whiteness

00:17:01.153 --> 00:17:04.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
you are associated with
all these different evils.

00:17:04.056 --> 00:17:05.491
These are moral evils.

00:17:05.491 --> 00:17:08.160 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's not the same as taking
like a physical thing

00:17:08.160 --> 00:17:11.563 align:start size:88% position:13%
because it doesn't
affect your moral value.

00:17:11.563 --> 00:17:12.631
That's the problem.

00:17:14.033 --> 00:17:18.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
- [George] The fact is
that I'm agreeing with you

00:17:19.738 --> 00:17:20.572 align:start size:84% position:16%
that there has
been a demonization

00:17:21.707 --> 00:17:24.543
that we need to get
our hands around

00:17:24.543 --> 00:17:27.646
in the way in which people
are doing this understanding.

00:17:27.646 --> 00:17:30.516
- [Paul] So you agree that
you were demonizing kids?

00:17:30.516 --> 00:17:35.521
- [George] We're demonizing
white people for being born.

00:17:36.955 --> 00:17:39.558
- [Paul] And are some of
our students white people?

00:17:39.558 --> 00:17:40.793
- [George] What?

00:17:40.793 --> 00:17:42.127
- [Paul] Are some of our
students white people?

00:17:42.127 --> 00:17:43.695
- [George] Yes

00:17:43.695 --> 00:17:45.764
- [Paul] Okay, so we're
demonizing white kids.

00:17:45.764 --> 00:17:47.066
Why don't you just say it?

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:51.570 align:start position:0%
- [George] We are using language
that them feel less than

00:17:51.570 --> 00:17:55.207
for nothing that they are
personally responsible for.

00:17:55.207 --> 00:17:57.209
- Okay, so that clip
is quite extraordinary

00:17:57.209 --> 00:18:01.213 align:start size:84% position:16%
because in essence
he's basically saying,

00:18:01.213 --> 00:18:03.415
yes, you're telling the truth.

00:18:03.415 --> 00:18:04.249
- Yes.

00:18:05.417 --> 00:18:07.553
- So you must have felt
kind of good, I guess,

00:18:07.553 --> 00:18:09.988
at that point that
you released it.

00:18:10.889 --> 00:18:12.458
- Yeah.

00:18:12.458 --> 00:18:13.926
I mean, if you back
me up against a wall

00:18:13.926 --> 00:18:17.729 align:start size:97% position:3%
and you call me a liar,
well, he left me no choice.

00:18:17.729 --> 00:18:19.865 align:start size:88% position:13%
I have a reputation
that I have to protect,

00:18:19.865 --> 00:18:21.033
especially since I'll probably

00:18:21.033 --> 00:18:22.634
be looking for another job soon.

00:18:24.036 --> 00:18:25.938 align:start size:81% position:19%
Additionally, I
want to make clear

00:18:25.938 --> 00:18:29.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the word
demonization was his word.

00:18:29.274 --> 00:18:31.410
I never suggested it to him.

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:35.714 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's why I was
actually quite shocked

00:18:35.714 --> 00:18:37.516
that he felt that way.

00:18:37.516 --> 00:18:40.018
And I was also shocked
that he hadn't taken

00:18:40.018 --> 00:18:42.888 align:start size:88% position:13%
any action on it because
what does it mean

00:18:42.888 --> 00:18:44.389
if the head of school knows

00:18:44.389 --> 00:18:47.659
that students are being
demonized for their race

00:18:47.659 --> 00:18:51.363 align:start size:88% position:13%
and does nothing except
share it privately

00:18:51.363 --> 00:18:54.233 align:start size:97% position:3%
and saying publicly something
completely different?

00:18:54.233 --> 00:18:57.703
So this was just, it
was gratifying in a way

00:18:57.703 --> 00:19:00.339 align:start size:97% position:3%
which is why it kind of
said, thank you, thank you.

00:19:00.339 --> 00:19:01.507
But it was also
really disturbing

00:19:01.507 --> 00:19:03.542
because nothing had been done

00:19:03.542 --> 00:19:05.944
or seemed would be
planned to be done.

00:19:05.944 --> 00:19:09.114 align:start size:88% position:13%
He did make some
mention about they were

00:19:09.114 --> 00:19:11.216
going to have a meeting
at the end of the year

00:19:11.216 --> 00:19:12.384
or something about it

00:19:12.384 --> 00:19:15.888 align:start size:84% position:16%
but that seemed
totally inappropriate

00:19:15.888 --> 00:19:18.757
to how serious the problem was.

00:19:18.757 --> 00:19:19.992
- Right.

00:19:19.992 --> 00:19:23.061 align:start size:84% position:16%
So to bring this all
to now, actually,

00:19:23.061 --> 00:19:24.263
so there was a little confusion,

00:19:24.263 --> 00:19:25.764
I think at first,

00:19:25.764 --> 00:19:28.634
whether you had been let go
or exactly what had happened.

00:19:28.634 --> 00:19:30.969 align:start size:84% position:16%
So you are still
employed by the school

00:19:30.969 --> 00:19:33.205
but they're just not
letting you teach,

00:19:33.205 --> 00:19:34.139
is that correct?

00:19:34.139 --> 00:19:36.241
- That's right, that's right.

00:19:36.241 --> 00:19:39.111
As of now, I still
have email access.

00:19:40.412 --> 00:19:43.081 align:start size:84% position:16%
I don't receive all
of the communications.

00:19:43.081 --> 00:19:44.850
I'm not on all the
distribution lists,

00:19:44.850 --> 00:19:48.020
as it turns out,
but at this point

00:19:48.020 --> 00:19:51.823
I still am connected to
the school in that way.

00:19:53.892 --> 00:19:56.628
I have been asked to
be on this task force

00:19:56.628 --> 00:19:58.597 align:start size:88% position:13%
but I think I've said
all I really need to say

00:19:58.597 --> 00:20:01.400
for them to work
it out themselves.

00:20:02.901 --> 00:20:03.969
Frankly, I don't
think there's much

00:20:03.969 --> 00:20:05.404
I need to add to that.

00:20:06.505 --> 00:20:08.307 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Do you think
there's any chance?

00:20:08.307 --> 00:20:09.741
I mean, they've sort
of just in essence

00:20:09.741 --> 00:20:11.577 align:start size:97% position:3%
doubled down, even now
after having him be exposed.

00:20:11.577 --> 00:20:13.512
I mean, do you sense
that there's any chance

00:20:13.512 --> 00:20:14.713 align:start size:84% position:16%
that they will
reverse any of this?

00:20:14.713 --> 00:20:15.948
Is there any evidence?

00:20:15.948 --> 00:20:17.950
I mean, this is one
of the key points

00:20:17.950 --> 00:20:19.251
of the whole woke thing.

00:20:19.251 --> 00:20:21.587
They don't seem to
respond to truth

00:20:21.587 --> 00:20:24.723 align:start size:84% position:16%
and almost in every
case they double down.

00:20:25.924 --> 00:20:27.459
- Yeah.

00:20:27.459 --> 00:20:29.895
They have put themselves in
a very precarious position.

00:20:29.895 --> 00:20:34.433 align:start position:0%
And you know the expression
between a rock and a hard place?

00:20:34.433 --> 00:20:35.867
Okay, this is like that,

00:20:35.867 --> 00:20:37.369
but instead of being crushed

00:20:37.369 --> 00:20:39.771
they're being pulled in
two opposite directions.

00:20:39.771 --> 00:20:44.743
So they've racialized
the atmosphere so much

00:20:45.978 --> 00:20:47.679
and promised so much
to different groups

00:20:47.679 --> 00:20:51.617 align:start size:84% position:16%
that now it's
almost like I wonder

00:20:51.617 --> 00:20:53.018
if they would, at this point,

00:20:53.018 --> 00:20:54.620
be able to reverse course,

00:20:54.620 --> 00:20:57.823 align:start size:88% position:13%
given how deeply they've
sunk their commitment

00:20:57.823 --> 00:21:00.859
into this divisive ideology.

00:21:02.261 --> 00:21:04.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know if it's a
problem that can be solved

00:21:05.897 --> 00:21:08.033 align:start size:81% position:19%
by changing course
at this point.

00:21:08.033 --> 00:21:09.067
- Right.

00:21:09.067 --> 00:21:10.535
In essence, they can't,

00:21:10.535 --> 00:21:11.803 align:start size:97% position:3%
because they've gone so
deep on teaching this stuff,

00:21:11.803 --> 00:21:14.273
that it would basically
point all of the light,

00:21:14.273 --> 00:21:16.074
shine all the light on them.

00:21:16.074 --> 00:21:18.977
So what do you want to
happen at this point?

00:21:18.977 --> 00:21:20.445
I mean, if you got an
email right now saying,

00:21:20.445 --> 00:21:23.715
hey, you can come teach
again, is that enough?

00:21:26.018 --> 00:21:27.552
- No, I want them
to change this.

00:21:27.552 --> 00:21:29.655
I want them to actually.

00:21:29.655 --> 00:21:31.089 align:start size:88% position:13%
I don't want the
school to be destroyed.

00:21:31.089 --> 00:21:33.859 align:start size:97% position:3%
I don't want to put vulnerable
students on the street.

00:21:33.859 --> 00:21:36.762
I want to simply allow for
greater viewpoint diversity,

00:21:36.762 --> 00:21:39.631
to have all students feel free

00:21:39.631 --> 00:21:41.033
to express their points of view

00:21:41.033 --> 00:21:43.068
and have them discussed openly

00:21:43.068 --> 00:21:46.538
in a spirit of open inquiry,

00:21:47.873 --> 00:21:50.575
not to have their
comments judged

00:21:50.575 --> 00:21:52.611 align:start size:84% position:16%
simply by the color
of their skin,

00:21:52.611 --> 00:21:54.713
which is what happens, I think.

00:21:54.713 --> 00:21:58.417 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
And with a lot of students,
their points of view

00:21:58.417 --> 00:22:02.888 line:0%
are labeled as one of group
of activist students labeled,

00:22:02.888 --> 00:22:04.356 line:0%
white opinions,

00:22:04.356 --> 00:22:06.725 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
simply because they're
uttered by a white person.

00:22:07.893 --> 00:22:10.796 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think they need
to completely revamp

00:22:10.796 --> 00:22:15.300 align:start position:0%
the entire culture of the school
to allow for open inquiry.

00:22:15.300 --> 00:22:18.337 align:start size:88% position:13%
And that's what students
have been asking for

00:22:20.405 --> 00:22:21.673
to me personally.

00:22:21.673 --> 00:22:24.209
So I think that's
really important.

00:22:24.209 --> 00:22:25.577 align:start size:84% position:16%
I don't want the
school to go bankrupt.

00:22:25.577 --> 00:22:28.447 align:start size:84% position:16%
I want the school
to be a good school,

00:22:28.447 --> 00:22:29.948
and that's how they could do it.

00:22:29.948 --> 00:22:33.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Are you shocked where
you've gotten some support

00:22:33.051 --> 00:22:35.754 align:start size:97% position:3%
and dismayed where you
haven't gotten some support?

00:22:37.222 --> 00:22:40.325
- I'm overwhelmed by how much
support I've gotten, frankly.

00:22:40.325 --> 00:22:45.330
I was expecting it to be like
half hate and half support.

00:22:47.099 --> 00:22:49.134
I would be happy if
that's what it was

00:22:49.134 --> 00:22:52.404 align:start size:97% position:3%
but I think the people
that have reached out to me

00:22:52.404 --> 00:22:54.539 align:start size:88% position:13%
have been overwhelmingly
supportive.

00:22:54.539 --> 00:22:57.876
Parents, alumni at
the school, students

00:22:57.876 --> 00:23:00.879 align:start size:88% position:13%
have said, "Thank you
so much for saying this.

00:23:00.879 --> 00:23:02.114
"Now that I'm in college,

00:23:02.114 --> 00:23:04.950
"I look back on my high
school and I feel like

00:23:04.950 --> 00:23:06.952 align:start size:84% position:16%
"I remember feeling
scared to say,

00:23:06.952 --> 00:23:09.788
"to express myself
in these classes."

00:23:11.123 --> 00:23:13.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think there are students
at the school now,

00:23:13.892 --> 00:23:15.594 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think there's a
substantial percentage

00:23:15.594 --> 00:23:18.497
of students at the school
now that are in support

00:23:18.497 --> 00:23:22.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
if not with my views,
with my right to speak up.

00:23:22.300 --> 00:23:24.770
And they have supported
my right to speak up.

00:23:26.338 --> 00:23:27.806 align:start size:97% position:3%
Now they can't do it
publicly, they're students.

00:23:27.806 --> 00:23:32.310
But I have ways that people
have communicated to me.

00:23:33.044 --> 00:23:35.714
So that inspires me,

00:23:35.714 --> 00:23:38.517
that actually gives
me a lot of hope

00:23:38.517 --> 00:23:40.919
that perhaps the worm is turning

00:23:40.919 --> 00:23:44.256
and we'll see some changes,

00:23:44.256 --> 00:23:47.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
if not at Grace, but maybe
in some other schools.

00:23:47.926 --> 00:23:49.428
We'll see.

00:23:49.428 --> 00:23:51.163
- Yeah. Well, as I said to
you right before we started,

00:23:51.163 --> 00:23:53.031
everyone that has
been on my show

00:23:53.031 --> 00:23:54.633
that I've seen step
through this thing

00:23:54.633 --> 00:23:55.834
and walk through that fire,

00:23:55.834 --> 00:23:58.103 align:start size:88% position:13%
they're always stronger
on the other side

00:23:58.103 --> 00:24:00.105 align:start size:97% position:3%
whether it's Bret Weinstein
or Lindsay Shepherd

00:24:00.105 --> 00:24:01.606
or even James Damore,

00:24:01.606 --> 00:24:03.809
anyone that's done it
from an academic angle

00:24:03.809 --> 00:24:06.378 align:start size:84% position:16%
or James did it
obviously at Google,

00:24:06.378 --> 00:24:08.046 align:start size:84% position:16%
whatever it is, if you
can get through it,

00:24:08.046 --> 00:24:09.281
then you're pretty much okay.

00:24:09.281 --> 00:24:11.183 align:start size:84% position:16%
If people want to find
out more about this

00:24:11.183 --> 00:24:12.984
or help you or reach out to you,

00:24:12.984 --> 00:24:15.420
as you said, you might be
looking for a job soon,

00:24:15.420 --> 00:24:17.489
where can we direct them?

00:24:17.489 --> 00:24:19.724
- You can email me at the email

00:24:19.724 --> 00:24:22.294
teachingfortruth@gmail.com.

00:24:23.695 --> 00:24:25.664
I am the only one that
has access to that email.

00:24:25.664 --> 00:24:27.999 align:start size:84% position:16%
No one else will see
what you send me,

00:24:27.999 --> 00:24:31.169 align:start position:0%
and I will keep every
everything confidential, if so.

00:24:31.169 --> 00:24:34.039
And I also respond to
every email that I get.

00:24:34.039 --> 00:24:35.273
So please reach me there.

00:24:35.273 --> 00:24:37.309
I'm also volunteering
currently for FAIR,

00:24:37.309 --> 00:24:40.545
the Foundation Against
Intolerance and Racism.

00:24:40.545 --> 00:24:45.016
And we're working to set
up chapters nationwide

00:24:45.016 --> 00:24:48.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
with parents and
students, and other people

00:24:48.954 --> 00:24:52.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
to basically push back and
create a common culture

00:24:52.557 --> 00:24:56.528 align:start size:97% position:3%
based on fairness,
understanding, and humanity.

00:24:56.528 --> 00:25:00.332
We have to get back to a
sane approach to education.

00:25:03.134 --> 00:25:04.970
And I think FAIR can help.

00:25:04.970 --> 00:25:06.404
- Yeah.

00:25:06.404 --> 00:25:08.773 align:start size:88% position:13%
And FAIR basically is
stepping into the vacuum

00:25:08.773 --> 00:25:10.642 align:start size:84% position:16%
where the ACLU
which unfortunately

00:25:10.642 --> 00:25:12.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
has kind of crumbled
under a lot of these ideas

00:25:12.377 --> 00:25:15.780
has just left the
range, so to speak.

00:25:15.780 --> 00:25:17.249
Well, Paul,

00:25:17.249 --> 00:25:19.584 align:start size:97% position:3%
I really appreciate you doing
this and I wish you luck.

00:25:19.584 --> 00:25:20.785
And if there's anything
I can do to help you

00:25:20.785 --> 00:25:23.088 align:start size:84% position:16%
along the ride,
please let me know.

00:25:23.088 --> 00:25:25.590
- I think you already have
Dave, this has been great.

00:25:25.590 --> 00:25:26.892
Thank you so much for having me.

00:25:26.892 --> 00:25:28.226
- All right, great. Thank you.

